    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9de2f67_9f15a4e2",
        "filename": "include/uapi/sound/compress_params.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 321,
      "author": {
        "id": 1293738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-25T17:59:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do wonder if you really need to make the below changes. Can\u0027t you just use SND_AUDIOCODEC_BESPOKE and define reserved[0] to an \"enum { WMA_PRO..DSD }\" and then alias the other 14 s32\u0027s to the fields you introduce below?\n\nIf you do it this way, you avoid updating SND_AUDIOCODEC_xxx and since BESPOKE was already defined by upstream, the HALs will continue to work even if upstream changes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "07a35bc4b84deadce0f799bec0ec9d77386e1ea8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b80746e9_2a3d7713",
        "filename": "include/uapi/sound/compress_params.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 321,
      "author": {
        "id": 1446383
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-25T18:14:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I took a closer look and I agree with what Alistair has to say. Another option is to try and upstream this as the new codecs you are adding seem fairly common/well known ones.\n\nAlso, keep in mind that if multiple vendors try to add their codecs, there\u0027s no way to decide who gets to keep their number and get the other to change theirs. So the best option seems to be to use BESPOKE where each vendor can define what those reserved bits mean inside their drivers.",
      "parentUuid": "b9de2f67_9f15a4e2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "07a35bc4b84deadce0f799bec0ec9d77386e1ea8",
